{
  "name": "scummvm010",
  "title": "ScummVM 0.10.0 (2007): thirteen engines -- SCUMM, Sky, Queen, Gob, Kyra, SAGA, AGOS, AGI, Cine, Touche, Parallaction, Broken Sword 1 and 2 -- C++ over SDL 1.2",
  "dir": "corpus/scummvm-0.10.0",
  "fetch": "curl -Lo /tmp/scummvm-0.10.0.tar.bz2 https://downloads.scummvm.org/frs/scummvm/0.10.0/scummvm-0.10.0.tar.bz2 && tar -xjf /tmp/scummvm-0.10.0.tar.bz2 -C corpus && node tools/scummvm010-configure.mjs",
  "_doc": "The release three years after 0.6.1 (targets/scummvm.json), studied as the upgrade of that build (P14.7). Its C++ is 0.6.1's and more: virtual bases (common/stream.h's Stream hierarchy), member templates (common/list.h's Node<T2> and Iterator<T2>), #pragma pack (common/pack-start.h), partial ordering of function templates, argument-dependent lookup of calls.",
  "_units": "Every object the release's Makefile builds with the configuration its configure writes: each module's MODULE_OBJS for the MODULES config.mk and engines/engines.mk select (the default engines; Lure and Cruise for a Corpse are off by default), printed by make itself (tools/scummvm010-configure.mjs, corpus/scummvm-0.10.0-generated/objs.json); gate-scummvm010 holds this list to it.",
